# The held-out BART-vs-linear comparison. Both arms, one split, one score.
#
# A COUNTRY split, not random: the measured note in docs is that a country RE carries essentially
# all the log-score skill, so a random split never tests an unseen region and reads ~20x more
# optimistic. If the question is whether BART on terrain GENERALISES, random cannot answer it.
#
# 8000 sweeps is the regime run_bart_gate.R documents for a held-out prediction comparison
# (~6000 retained). It is NOT enough to read sigma_v or its intervals off.
# The design must NOT carry coordinates: the gate appends its own lon/lat, and a dump built with
# DRIVER_ADD_COORDS would end up with the scaled pair in the LINEAR arm. Use the plain GLOBIOM
# design, not pixel_model_inputs_GLOBIOM_bartrecon.rds (which exists for the recovery task).
SPLIT=country
TESTFRAC=0.2
ARMS=linear,bart
NITER=8000
NBURN=2000
THIN=8
N_CHAINS=1
SUBSAMPLE=0
